    "long_instructions": "`generate` returns a list of tokens, like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[\"The\", \"proof\", \"is\", \"always\", \"right\", \".\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo print it as a sentence, you need to turn the list back into a single string. The `detokenize` function should do just that.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Complete the `detokenize` function.\r\n  - Join the tokens in `tokens` into a single string, with a space between each token.\r\n  - Replace `\" .\"` with `\".\"` so the period sits at the end of the last word.\r\n  - Return the resulting string.\r\n\r\n💻 Coding Tip\r\n\r\n`\" \".join` combines a list of strings into one string, with a space between each item.\r\n\r\n```\r\n\" \".join([\"The\", \"proof\", \"is\"]) # \"The proof is\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n`replace` returns a copy of a string with every match swapped out:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"Hello world .\".replace(\" .\", \".\")\r\n```\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "A collection of short sayings that express some truth.",
